test notes -- equivalence suite hardening
=========================================
- The reference checkout moved: the repository itself was rewritten, so
  ``../flash-kmeans`` no longer contains the Triton kernels.  The tests now
  resolve the reference from ``FLASH_KMEANS_REF_REPO`` or a dedicated
  sibling checkout (``flash-kmeans-upstream``, created with
  ``git worktree add ../flash-kmeans-upstream <pre-rewrite commit>``) and
  validate that ``assign_euclid_triton.py`` really imports triton before
  using it.
- The large-N comparison now uses well-separated Gaussian blobs.  With
  uniform random data every point is a near-tie, so two implementations with
  different accumulation orders drift apart after two iterations and the
  label-agreement thresholds were flaky (1-in-3 failures observed).
- The large-N vs batch test compares the reached objective (inertia) as the
  primary criterion, with label agreement and the centroid delta as sanity
  bounds.
